  ["new repo kotoba-lang/i18n: portable .cljc i18n library (message registry, defmessages compile-time accessors, CLDR-lite plural rules, RTL/tier language registry, etzhayyim TM-service JSON bridge, shitsuke-seam re-frame/reagent integration)"
   "i18n.core/plural/registry/messages/tm-import are zero third-party runtime deps (mirrors dot/jsonlogic/toml); only i18n.re-frame/i18n.reagent depend on shitsuke"
   "defmessages macro is the paraglide-js equivalent for cljc: reads an EDN catalog at macroexpansion time, emits one defn per key calling i18n.core/t (key set fixed at compile time, translated text stays a runtime lookup so set-locale! needs no rebuild)"
   "select-map plural/gender branching ({:select :count :one ... :other ...}) is Fluent-inspired, mirroring what paraglide v2's own match/when syntax already borrows from Project Fluent"
   "i18n.tm-import is a pure data-shape bridge (flat dotted-key JSON <-> namespaced-keyword catalog; GetLanguageRegistry response -> i18n.registry/load! entries) with no HTTP client of its own — i18n.etzhayyim.com stays the system of record for LLM translation + human-approval QA"
   "i18n.reagent/locale-links + wire-lang-switch! generalize the delegated a[data-lang] click-listener pattern already proven by kami-mangaka-reader/src/kami/mangaka/reader/app.cljs"]
